        "date": "2026-11-20T09:35:57Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): show the operator side at the work envelope\n\nThe work envelope gets an arrow on the operator side and the text\n\"Operator side\". The arrow starts at the lower edge of the envelope\nand points out of it, toward the operator.\n\n- camcraft-post: a machine file may state `general.operator_side`\n  (\"-X\", \"+X\", \"-Y\", \"+Y\"). The field is optional, so old files and\n  old projects load unchanged. A wrong word refuses the file by name.\n  `OperatorSide::default_for` gives the default of each machine kind:\n  +Y for a lathe, -Y for each other kind.\n- camcraft-ui: `operator_side` builds the arrow when its input changes\n  (the placed envelope and the side) and keeps it for each other frame.\n  The text is screen text at the tip. The View door has the switch\n  \"Show operator side\" (view state, on by default, no command).\n- docs: the machine file grammar and the decision file.\n\nStacked on #2835 (the same lines of `view_menu`).\n\nFixes #2632\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
